The code of this layer (recipes, classes, scripts, the library ps2gl, the
demos and the tools) is under the MIT license below.

The patches under recipes-*/*/files/*.patch change other projects and
carry the license of the project they change: the Linux kernel, GCC,
binutils, glibc and the IOP modules of iopmod are GPL-2.0 or later as
each file says, libffi is MIT, SDL2 is Zlib. The kernel module snd-ps2
and the IOP module spu2 are GPL-2.0-only, as their source files say.

The games are separate projects under their own licenses, fetched at
build time. Their data files are not part of this layer.

Files with a credit of their own: tests/pcsx2check.cpp of the library is
built with headers of the PCSX2 emulator and is GPL-3.0-or-later; the VU1
simulator tests/vusim.c is a new implementation of the rules read in the
PCSX2 interpreter; the sound module and its LIBSD import header follow
the libsd and audsrv sources of ps2sdk (Academic Free License 2.0); the
Doom platform file follows doomgeneric (GPL-2.0). Each file says so in
its header. The README has the list of the projects this layer builds
on.

